{"title": "Sectional Mock #19 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A certain sum amounts to &#8377;3240 in two years and &#8377;3888 in three years at R% rate of compound interest. Find the rate of interest, when the interest is compounded annually.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; R% &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;3240 &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;3888 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2348; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10%", "20%", "8%", "15%"], "options_hi": ["10%", "20%", "8%", "15%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question-</p><p>P(1 + R/100)<sup>2</sup> = 3240 ----(1)</p><p>P(1 + R/100)<sup>3</sup> = 3888 ----(2)</p><p>On dividing (2) by (1)  - </p><p>1 + R/100 = 3888/3240 = 6/5</p><p>R = 100/5</p><p>R = 20%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question-</p><p>P(1 + R/100)<sup>2</sup> = 3240 ----(1)</p><p>P(1 + R/100)<sup>3</sup> = 3888 ----(2)</p><p>On dividing (2) by (1)  - </p><p>1 + R/100 = 3888/3240 = 6/5</p><p>R = 100/5</p><p>R = 20%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sudarsan and Abraham appear for an interview for two vacancies. The probability of Sudarsan's selection is 1/3 and that of Abraham's selection is 1/5. Find the probability that none of them be selected.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2350; &#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; 1/3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; 1/5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2368; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8/15", "14/15", "1/15", "22/15"], "options_hi": ["8/15", "14/15", "1/15", "22/15"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Probability of Sudarsan's selection = 1/3</p><p>probability of Abraham's selection = 1/5</p><p>P(Sudarsan not selected) = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3</p><p>P(Abraham not selected) = 1 - 1/5 = 4/5</p><p>P(none) = 2/3 * 4/5 = 8/15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Probability of Sudarsan's selection = 1/3</p><p>probability of Abraham's selection = 1/5</p><p>P(Sudarsan not selected) = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3</p><p>P(Abraham not selected) = 1 - 1/5 = 4/5</p><p>P(none) = 2/3 * 4/5 = 8/15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two points K and L are on a river and river is flowing along KL. If a boat rows from point L to point K in 2 hours and rows from point K to point L in 4/7 hours less time than it takes to cover from point L to point K, then what is the speed of the boat? (KL = 30 km)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; K &#2324;&#2352; L &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2342;&#2368; KL &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2342;&#2367;&#2358; &#2348;&#2361; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; L &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; K &#2340;&#2325; 2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; K &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; L &#2340;&#2325; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; L &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; K &#2340;&#2325; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 4/7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;? (KL = 30 km)</p>", "options_en": ["28 km/h", "36 km/h", "9 km/h", "18 km/h"], "options_hi": ["28 km/h", "36 km/h", "9 km/h", "18 km/h"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Upstream speed of the boat = 30/2 = 15 km/h</p><p>And downstream speed of the boat = 30/(2  -  4/7) = 21 km/h</p><p>So, speed of the boat in still water = (21 + 15)/2 = 18 km/h</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Upstream speed of the boat = 30/2 = 15 km/h</p><p>And downstream speed of the boat = 30/(2  -  4/7) = 21 km/h</p><p>So, speed of the boat in still water = (21 + 15)/2 = 18 km/h</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two numbers are in the ratio of 9: 11. If 7 is added to the smaller number and 8 is added to the larger number, then the ratio becomes 5: 6. What would be the ratio when 12 is subtracted from a smaller number and 6 is subtracted from a larger number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 5:6 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 12 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["3: 8", "4: 7", "1: 2", "2: 3"], "options_hi": ["3: 8", "4: 7", "1: 2", "2: 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the smaller number = 9x and the larger number = 11x</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(9x + 7)/(11x + 8) = 5/6</p><p>54x + 42 = 55x + 40</p><p>X = 2</p><p>Smaller number = 18 and larger number = 22</p><p>Required ratio = (18  -  12): (22  -  6) = 6: 16 = 3: 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the smaller number = 9x and the larger number = 11x</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(9x + 7)/(11x + 8) = 5/6</p><p>54x + 42 = 55x + 40</p><p>X = 2</p><p>Smaller number = 18 and larger number = 22</p><p>Required ratio = (18  -  12): (22  -  6) = 6: 16 = 3: 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the base of a right pyramid is a triangle of sides 9 cm, 40 cm, and 41 cm and its volume is 2100 cm<sup>3</sup>, then find its height?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; 9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 41 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; 2100 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["33 cm", "29 cm", "27 cm", "35 cm"], "options_hi": ["33 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The given base is a triangle with sides 9 cm, 40 cm, and 41 cm.</p><p>Since 9<sup>2</sup> + 40<sup>2 </sup>= 41<sup>2</sup>, it is a right triangle with the following:</p><p>Base = 9 cm, Height = 40 cm, Hypotenuse = 41 cm</p><p>The area of a right triangle = 1/2  X  Base  X  Height</p><p>= 1/2 * 9 * 40</p><p>= 180 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * area of base * height</p><p>2100 = 1/3  X  180  X  h</p><p>h = 35 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The given base is a triangle with sides 9 cm, 40 cm, and 41 cm.</p><p>Since 9<sup>2</sup> + 40<sup>2 </sup>= 41<sup>2</sup>, it is a right triangle with the following:</p><p>Base = 9 cm, Height = 40 cm, Hypotenuse = 41 cm</p><p>The area of a right triangle = 1/2  X  Base  X  Height</p><p>= 1/2 * 9 * 40</p><p>= 180 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * area of base * height</p><p>2100 = 1/3  X  180  X  h</p><p>h = 35 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Using empirical formula, calculate the mode for the following data.</p><p>17, 20, 21, 18, 25, 28, 24, 22, 16, 24, 25, 24</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2357;&#2332;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375;, &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>17, 20, 21, 18, 25, 28, 24, 22, 16, 24, 25, 24</p>", "options_en": ["25.8", "32", "25", "30.6"], "options_hi": ["25.8", "32", "25", "30.6"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Empirical formula: Mode = 3  X  Median - 2  X  Mean</p><p><b>Median:</b></p><p>Order: 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, 22, 24, 24, 24, 25, 25, 28</p><p>n = 12, median = (6th + 7th) / 2 = (22 + 24) / 2 = 23</p><p><b>Mean:</b></p><p>Sum = 16 + 17 + 18 + 20 + 21 + 22 + 24 + 24 + 24 + 25 + 25 + 28 = 264</p><p>Mean = 264 / 12 = 22</p><p><b>Mode:</b></p><p>Mode = 3  X  23 - 2  X  22 = 69 - 44 = 25</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Empirical formula: Mode = 3  X  Median - 2  X  Mean</p><p><b>Median:</b></p><p>Order: 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, 22, 24, 24, 24, 25, 25, 28</p><p>n = 12, median = (6th + 7th) / 2 = (22 + 24) / 2 = 23</p><p><b>Mean:</b></p><p>Sum = 16 + 17 + 18 + 20 + 21 + 22 + 24 + 24 + 24 + 25 + 25 + 28 = 264</p><p>Mean = 264 / 12 = 22</p><p><b>Mode:</b></p><p>Mode = 3  X  23 - 2  X  22 = 69 - 44 = 25</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p> If 1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + -------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> = 385, then 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ----- + 30 <sup>2</sup> is equal to </p><p> </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + -------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> = 385, &#2340;&#2379; 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ----- + 30 <sup>2</sup> &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["2310", "3465", "1155", "770"], "options_hi": ["2310", "3465", "1155", "770"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 30 <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r (3 &#215; 1) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 2) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 3) <sup>2</sup> + ------- + (3 &#215; 10) <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 [1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> ]</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 &#215; 385 </p><p>= 3465</p><p></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 3 <sup>2</sup> + 6 <sup>2</sup> + 9 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 30 <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r (3 &#215; 1) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 2) <sup>2</sup> + (3 &#215; 3) <sup>2</sup> + ------- + (3 &#215; 10) <sup>2</sup></p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 [1 <sup>2</sup> + 2 <sup>2</sup> + 3 <sup>2</sup> + ------- + 10 <sup>2</sup> ]</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005070.png\"/>\r 9 &#215; 385 </p><p>= 3465</p><p></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Triangle PQR is a right  -  angled triangle at Q. If cotP = 9/40, then cosP  -  cosQ + cosR will be equal to -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; PQR, Q &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cotP = 9/40, &#2340;&#2379; cosP - cosQ + cosR &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; -</p>", "options_en": ["1(7/41)", "1(3/41)", "1(6/41)", "1(8/41)"], "options_hi": ["1(7/41)", "1(3/41)", "1(6/41)", "1(8/41)"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=169 height=146 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26460/image008.png\"></p><p>Triangle PQR is a right  -  angled triangle at Q, i.e.</p><p>PR = hypotenuse</p><p>cotP = B/P = 9/40</p><p>P = 9, B = 40</p><p>PR = Hypotenuse = &radic;(9<sup>2</sup> + 40<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 41</p><p>cosP  -  cosQ + cosR</p><p>= cosP  -  cos90&deg; + cosR</p><p>= 9/41  -  0 + 40/41</p><p>= 49/41</p><p>= 1(8/41)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=169 height=146 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p26460/image008.png\"></p><p>Triangle PQR is a right  -  angled triangle at Q, i.e.</p><p>PR = hypotenuse</p><p>cotP = B/P = 9/40</p><p>P = 9, B = 40</p><p>PR = Hypotenuse = &radic;(9<sup>2</sup> + 40<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 41</p><p>cosP  -  cosQ + cosR</p><p>= cosP  -  cos90&deg; + cosR</p><p>= 9/41  -  0 + 40/41</p><p>= 49/41</p><p>= 1(8/41)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 3(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>) = (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> and a, b, c are non-zero real numbers, then</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 3(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>) = (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; a, b, c &#2327;&#2376;&#2352;-&#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379;-</p>", "options_en": ["a + b = c", "a + c = b", "b + c = a", "a = b =c"], "options_hi": ["a + b = c", "a + c = b", "b + c = a", "a = b =c"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>3(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>) = (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup></p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> + 3b<sup>2</sup> + 3c<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + 2bc + 2ca</p><p>2a<sup>2</sup> + 2b<sup>2</sup> + 2c<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab  -  2bc  -  2ca = 0</p><p>[(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> + (b  -  c)<sup>2</sup> + (c  -  a)<sup>2</sup>] = 0</p><p>Therefore, a = b = c</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>) = (a + b + c)<sup>2</sup></p><p>3a<sup>2</sup> + 3b<sup>2</sup> + 3c<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + 2bc + 2ca</p><p>2a<sup>2</sup> + 2b<sup>2</sup> + 2c<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab  -  2bc  -  2ca = 0</p><p>[(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> + (b  -  c)<sup>2</sup> + (c  -  a)<sup>2</sup>] = 0</p><p>Therefore, a = b = c</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>In an alloy, silver, and copper are in the ratio 7/11. In the second alloy, the same elements are in the ratio of 13: 11. If these two alloys are mixed to form a new alloy in which two elements are in the ratio of 7:8, the ratio of these two alloys in the new alloy is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2330;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; 7/11 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2357;&#2361;&#2368; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; 13:11 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2312; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; 7:8 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2312; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["27: 28", "31: 30", "27: 26", "29: 26"], "options_hi": ["27: 28", "31: 30", "27: 26", "29: 26"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=313 height=108 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27152/image003.png\"></p><p>9/120 7/90</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = (9/120)/(7/90) = 27: 28</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=313 height=108 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27152/image003.png\"></p><p>9/120 7/90</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = (9/120)/(7/90) = 27: 28</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>Average of three integers L, M and N is 843 and average of M and N is 750. If M is 129 less than L, then the value of N is -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; L, M &#2324;&#2352; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 843 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; M &#2324;&#2352; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 750 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; M, L &#2360;&#2375; 129 &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376; -</p>", "options_en": ["817", "920", "600", "724"], "options_hi": ["817", "920", "600", "724"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Since M is 129 less than L-</p><p>L = M + 129</p><p>L + M + N = 3*843 = 2529</p><p>M + 129 + M + N = 2529</p><p>2M + N = 2400 ------(1)</p><p>M + N = 2*750 = 1500 ----(2)</p><p>From (1) and (2)-</p><p>N = 600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since M is 129 less than L-</p><p>L = M + 129</p><p>L + M + N = 3*843 = 2529</p><p>M + 129 + M + N = 2529</p><p>2M + N = 2400 ------(1)</p><p>M + N = 2*750 = 1500 ----(2)</p><p>From (1) and (2)-</p><p>N = 600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>If cosq=4/5, find the value of cotq+tanq.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cosq=4/5 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; cotq+tanq &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["12/25", "25/12", "27/12", "12/27"], "options_hi": ["12/25", "25/12", "27/12", "12/27"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>cosq=4/5 = Base/Hypotenuse</p><p>Perpendicular = &radic;[Hypotenuse<sup>2</sup>  -  Base<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;(5<sup>2</sup>  -  4<sup>2</sup>) = 3</p><p>cot&#952; = Base/Perpendicular = 3/4</p><p>tan&#952; = Perpendicular/Base = 4/3</p><p>cotq + tanq.</p><p>= 3/4 + 4/3</p><p>= (9 + 16)/12</p><p>= 25/12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cosq=4/5 = Base/Hypotenuse</p><p>Perpendicular = &radic;[Hypotenuse<sup>2</sup>  -  Base<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;(5<sup>2</sup>  -  4<sup>2</sup>) = 3</p><p>cot&#952; = Base/Perpendicular = 3/4</p><p>tan&#952; = Perpendicular/Base = 4/3</p><p>cotq + tanq.</p><p>= 3/4 + 4/3</p><p>= (9 + 16)/12</p><p>= 25/12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 3a + 2b = 27 and 27a<sup>3 </sup>+ 8b<sup>3 </sup>= 1458, then find 2ab.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 3a + 2b = 27 &#2324;&#2352; 27a<sup>3 </sup>+ 8b<sup>3 </sup>= 1458, &#2340;&#2379; 2ab &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["72", "70", "77", "75"], "options_hi": ["72", "70", "77", "75"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>As we know,</p><p>(3a + 2b)<sup>3</sup> = 27a<sup>3</sup> + 8b<sup>3</sup> + 3 * 3a * 2b(3a + 2b)</p><p>27<sup>3</sup> = 1458 + 18ab * 27</p><p>=&gt; 19683 = 1458 + 486ab</p><p>=&gt; 19683 - 1458 = 486ab</p><p>=&gt; 18225 = 486ab</p><p>=&gt; ab = 18225 / 486</p><p>=&gt; ab = 37.5</p><p>=&gt; 2ab = 2  X  37.5</p><p>=&gt; 2ab = 75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As we know,</p><p>(3a + 2b)<sup>3</sup> = 27a<sup>3</sup> + 8b<sup>3</sup> + 3 * 3a * 2b(3a + 2b)</p><p>27<sup>3</sup> = 1458 + 18ab * 27</p><p>=&gt; 19683 = 1458 + 486ab</p><p>=&gt; 19683 - 1458 = 486ab</p><p>=&gt; 18225 = 486ab</p><p>=&gt; ab = 18225 / 486</p><p>=&gt; ab = 37.5</p><p>=&gt; 2ab = 2  X  37.5</p><p>=&gt; 2ab = 75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A 180 litres solution of acid and water contains 40% acid. How much water (in litres) must be added to get a solution to having 25% acid? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; 180 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40% &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 25% &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; (&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["108 l", "96 l", "112 l", "90 l"], "options_hi": ["108 &#2354;&#2368;", "96 &#2319;&#2354;", "112 &#2319;&#2354;", "90 &#2354;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Acid = 180 * 40/100 = 72 l </p><p>Water = 180  -  72 = 108 l</p><p>Let the quantity of water added be 'X' l</p><p>(180 + X) * 25/100 = 72 </p><p>180 + X = 288 </p><p>X = 108 l </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Acid = 180 * 40/100 = 72 l </p><p>Water = 180  -  72 = 108 l</p><p>Let the quantity of water added be 'X' l</p><p>(180 + X) * 25/100 = 72 </p><p>180 + X = 288 </p><p>X = 108 l </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B together can complete a work in 5 days, B and C together can complete it in 10 days and C and A together can complete it in 20 days. Find the time taken by B alone to complete the work.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 5 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 10 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; C &#2324;&#2352; A &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 20 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8 days", "10 days", "12 days", "6 days"], "options_hi": ["8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "10 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "12 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "6 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total work = LCM of 5, 10 and 20 = 20 units</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B) = 20/5 = 4 units</p><p>Efficiency of (B + C) = 20/10 = 2 units</p><p>Efficiency of (C + A) = 20/20 = 1 unit</p><p>Efficiency of 2(A + B + C) = 7 units</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B + C) = 3.5 units</p><p>Subtracting efficiency of A and C together from efficiency of A, B and C together, we get -</p><p>3.5  -  1 = 2.5 unit </p><p>Required time = 20/2.5 = 8 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total work = LCM of 5, 10 and 20 = 20 units</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B) = 20/5 = 4 units</p><p>Efficiency of (B + C) = 20/10 = 2 units</p><p>Efficiency of (C + A) = 20/20 = 1 unit</p><p>Efficiency of 2(A + B + C) = 7 units</p><p>Efficiency of (A + B + C) = 3.5 units</p><p>Subtracting efficiency of A and C together from efficiency of A, B and C together, we get -</p><p>3.5  -  1 = 2.5 unit </p><p>Required time = 20/2.5 = 8 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>A seller decreased the selling price of each item from 6000 to 5640, by which his loss percentage increased by 8%. If he has to get 8% profit, then the selling price of the item should be:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 6000 &#2360;&#2375; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 5640 &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 8% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 8% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 4500", "Rs. 4680", "Rs. 4860", "Rs. 4200"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 4500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4680", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4860", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4200"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. X</p><p>Loss% = (C.P  -  S.P) * 100/C. P</p><p>Initial loss % = (X  -  6000) * 100/X</p><p>Final loss % = (X  -  5640) * 100/X </p><p>Initial loss + 8 = Final loss</p><p>(X  -  6000) * 100/X + 8 = (X  -  5640) * 100/X</p><p>100X  -  564000  -  100X + 600000 = 8X </p><p>8X = 36000</p><p>X = 4500 </p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 4500 * 108/100 = Rs. 4860 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let C.P. be Rs. X</p><p>Loss% = (C.P  -  S.P) * 100/C. P</p><p>Initial loss % = (X  -  6000) * 100/X</p><p>Final loss % = (X  -  5640) * 100/X </p><p>Initial loss + 8 = Final loss</p><p>(X  -  6000) * 100/X + 8 = (X  -  5640) * 100/X</p><p>100X  -  564000  -  100X + 600000 = 8X </p><p>8X = 36000</p><p>X = 4500 </p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 4500 * 108/100 = Rs. 4860 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>X and Y borrowed &#8377;22260 each from Z. They returned the amount in two equal installments at 10% and 12% at rate of simple interest respectively. Find the difference between interest received by Z from both X and Y.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2344;&#2375; Z &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;22260 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 10% &#2324;&#2352; 12% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2380;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; Z &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;740", "&#8377;500", "&#8377;600", "&#8377;450"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;740", "&#8377;500", "&#8377;600", "&#8377;450"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let each installment for X and Y be &#8377;x and &#8377;y respectively.</p><p>22260*[1 + (10*2/100)] = x[1 + (10*1/100)] + x</p><p>22260*120 = 210x</p><p>x = &#8377;12720</p><p>22260*[1 + (12*2/100)] = y[1 + (12*1/100)] + y</p><p>22260*124 = 212y</p><p>y = &#8377;13020</p><p>Interest received from X = 2*12720  -  22260 = &#8377;3180</p><p>Interest received from Y = 2*13020  -  22260 = &#8377;3780</p><p>Required difference = 3780  -  3180 = &#8377;600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let each installment for X and Y be &#8377;x and &#8377;y respectively.</p><p>22260*[1 + (10*2/100)] = x[1 + (10*1/100)] + x</p><p>22260*120 = 210x</p><p>x = &#8377;12720</p><p>22260*[1 + (12*2/100)] = y[1 + (12*1/100)] + y</p><p>22260*124 = 212y</p><p>y = &#8377;13020</p><p>Interest received from X = 2*12720  -  22260 = &#8377;3180</p><p>Interest received from Y = 2*13020  -  22260 = &#8377;3780</p><p>Required difference = 3780  -  3180 = &#8377;600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>There is a path around a circular field and ratio of radius of circular field to the width of the path is 4: 1. If area of the path is 346.5 cm<sup>2</sup>, then find the radius of the field?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 346.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["28 cm", "30 cm", "14 cm", "20 cm"], "options_hi": ["28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let radius of the circular field is '4x' cm and width of the path is 'x' cm.</p><p>So, distance of outer line of the path from centre of the field = 4x + x = '5x' cm</p><p>From the question:</p><p>(22/7) * (25x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = 346.5</p><p>(22/7) * 9x<sup>2</sup> = 346.5</p><p>x = 3.5</p><p>Radius of the field = 4 * 3.5 = 14 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let radius of the circular field is '4x' cm and width of the path is 'x' cm.</p><p>So, distance of outer line of the path from centre of the field = 4x + x = '5x' cm</p><p>From the question:</p><p>(22/7) * (25x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = 346.5</p><p>(22/7) * 9x<sup>2</sup> = 346.5</p><p>x = 3.5</p><p>Radius of the field = 4 * 3.5 = 14 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Per capita water requirement in a small town is 120 litres/person. The population of the town is estimated to grow at a rate of 10% per year. If, the current population of the town is 45000, how much water per day will be required to meet the demand 3 years from now?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; 120 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367;, &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 45000 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 3 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["6587.4 kilo litres/day", "8587.4 kilo litres/day", "6187.4 kilo litres/day", "7187.4 kilo litres/day"], "options_hi": ["6587.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "8587.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "6187.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "7187.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=448 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=432 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image010.png\"></p><p>Water demand 3 years later for the increased population = 59895  X  120 = 7187400 litres = 7187.4 kilo litres/day</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=448 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=432 height=48 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20559/image010.png\"></p><p>Water demand 3 years later for the increased population = 59895  X  120 = 7187400 litres = 7187.4 kilo litres/day</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The probabilities of solving a problem by three friends A, B, and C are 4/9, 7/12, and 5/11 respectively. The probability that the problem will be solved is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4/9, 7/12 &#2324;&#2352; 5/11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["25/198", "81/198", "173/198", "95/198"], "options_hi": ["25/198", "81/198", "173/198", "95/198"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>P(A') = 1  -  4/9 = 5/9 </p><p>P(B') = 1  -  7/12 = 5/12 </p><p>P(C') = 1  -  5/11 = 6/11 </p><p>Probability of encoding = 5/9 * 5/12 * 6/11 = 25/198 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1  -  25/198 = 173/198</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P(A') = 1  -  4/9 = 5/9 </p><p>P(B') = 1  -  7/12 = 5/12 </p><p>P(C') = 1  -  5/11 = 6/11 </p><p>Probability of encoding = 5/9 * 5/12 * 6/11 = 25/198 </p><p>Hence, the required probability = 1  -  25/198 = 173/198</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Probability"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two poles of heights 10 m and 17 m are fixed to a level ground. The distance between the bottom of the poles is 24 m. What is the distance (in m) between their tops?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>10 m &#2324;&#2352; 17 m &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2354; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 24 m &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (m &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["25", "24", "30", "27"], "options_hi": ["25", "24", "30", "27"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=266 height=220 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image044.png\"></p><p>Since AB = DC</p><p>So, DE = 17  -  10 = 7 m</p><p>And BC = AD = 24 m</p><p>In &#916;ADE,</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = AD<sup>2</sup> + DE<sup>2</sup> (Using Pythagoras theorem)</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = 24<sup>2</sup> + 7<sup>2</sup></p><p>AE<sup>2 </sup>= 576 + 49</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = 625</p><p>AE = 25 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=266 height=220 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19993/image044.png\"></p><p>Since AB = DC</p><p>So, DE = 17  -  10 = 7 m</p><p>And BC = AD = 24 m</p><p>In &#916;ADE,</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = AD<sup>2</sup> + DE<sup>2</sup> (Using Pythagoras theorem)</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = 24<sup>2</sup> + 7<sup>2</sup></p><p>AE<sup>2 </sup>= 576 + 49</p><p>AE<sup>2</sup> = 625</p><p>AE = 25 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Solution A contains x% alcohol and Solution B contains (x + 10)% alcohol. When they are mixed in the ratio 2:3, the mixture contains 42% alcohol. What is the value of x?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; x% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; (x + 10)% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2332;&#2348; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; 2:3 &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 42% &#2309;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2377;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["32", "36", "34", "38"], "options_hi": ["32", "36", "34", "38"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>(2x + 3(x + 10))/5 = 42</p><p>5x + 30 = 210</p><p>5x = 180</p><p>x = 36</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>(2x + 3(x + 10))/5 = 42</p><p>5x + 30 = 210</p><p>5x = 180</p><p>x = 36</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many factors of 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup> are divisible by 42 but not by 84?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; 42 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; 84 &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["48", "24", "36", "12"], "options_hi": ["48", "24", "36", "12"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>42 = 2 * 3 * 7</p><p>84 = 2<sup>2</sup> * 3 * 7</p><p>Now, to have number divisible by 42 and not by 84. We have to make sure that 2 is taken only once. As, if we pick 2 two's, then it will form 84 with no. of 3 and 7 selected and since minimum 3 and 7 we have to select is 1, we cannot have 2 more than one.</p><p>Number= 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup></p><p>So, there are 2 ways of picking 3, 8 ways of picking 3, 3 ways of picking 7 and only one way of picking 2 and that is 2<sup>1</sup>.</p><p>So, total number of ways = 1 * 2 * 8 * 3 = 48</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>42 = 2 * 3 * 7</p><p>84 = 2<sup>2</sup> * 3 * 7</p><p>Now, to have number divisible by 42 and not by 84. We have to make sure that 2 is taken only once. As, if we pick 2 two's, then it will form 84 with no. of 3 and 7 selected and since minimum 3 and 7 we have to select is 1, we cannot have 2 more than one.</p><p>Number= 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> * 5<sup>7</sup> * 7<sup>3</sup></p><p>So, there are 2 ways of picking 3, 8 ways of picking 3, 3 ways of picking 7 and only one way of picking 2 and that is 2<sup>1</sup>.</p><p>So, total number of ways = 1 * 2 * 8 * 3 = 48</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If each observation of the data is increased by 7.55, then what is the effect on the mean?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2357;&#2354;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357; &#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["increased by 75.5", "decreased by 6.55", "decreased by 72.5", "increased by 7.55"], "options_hi": ["75.5 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;", "6.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368;", "72.5 &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;", "7.55 &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>When each observation of the data is increased by X, then mean is also increased by X.</p><p>So, mean will be increased by 7.55.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When each observation of the data is increased by X, then mean is also increased by X.</p><p>So, mean will be increased by 7.55.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>A metal cuboid of dimensions 56 cm * 55 cm * 70 cm is drawn into a cylindrical wire of radius 7 cm. Find the length of the wire.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; 56 cm * 55 cm * 70 cm &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; 7 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366; (&#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2366;) &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18.8 m", "10 m", "12.4 m", "14 m"], "options_hi": ["18.8 m", "10 m", "12.4 m", "14 m"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cuboid = Volume of cylindrical wire</p><p>56 * 55 * 70 = &#960; * 7<sup>2</sup> * h</p><p>h = <img width=84 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20967/image016.png\"></p><p>h = 1400 cm</p><p>h = 14 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cuboid = Volume of cylindrical wire</p><p>56 * 55 * 70 = &#960; * 7<sup>2</sup> * h</p><p>h = <img width=84 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20967/image016.png\"></p><p>h = 1400 cm</p><p>h = 14 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}]}